#---
# purpose: "a spawned process that throws with no catch prints the throw line and ends; main carries on and the program exits 0"
# oracle: 00812_a_throw_in_a_spawned_process_prints_its_line_and_main_carries_on.oracle.exs
#---
# Elixir reports the spawned throw through its logger as an ErlangError
# wrapping {:nocatch, :child_ball}; fz prints the throw line, on stderr. The
# oracle silences the logger so its stdout is the program's own output.
def main() do
  parent = self()
  spawn(fn () ->
    send(parent, :child_started)
    throw(:child_ball)
  end)
  receive do
    message -> dbg(message)
  end
  dbg(:main_carried_on)
end
